A fieldRules `error` on a blocks region (a rule counting its children, e.g. "at least two") now blocks the save, and says why: the refused save's toast names the field and gives the message (it read "Template Error" with no text for any schema error), and the block's settings show the region's error at the top, beside the warnings — a region has no widget of its own to turn red. Volto validates a field only when `formData[field]` has a value, and a region's children live in `blocks_layout`, so the error had reached the content validator and never the save.
